"""MOOD V3 Specialty catalog: the 98 curated exercise additions (93 standalone + 5 programming-layer complexes).

Additive to the frozen Strength exercise library -- never edits it. Standalone entries here follow the exact
production tagging schema (movement pattern / primary+secondary muscles / equipment / skill / complexity) used by
`engines/strength/audit_engine.EX`, so the specialty adapter can reason about them the same way the frozen engine
reasons about its own library. Where a curated addition is already in the frozen production library, the specialty
pool references that exercise BY ID instead of duplicating it (see `engines/specialty/adapter.py:production_pool_for`).

`media_status`:
  'production_ready' -- has a real, hosted thumbnail/image (verified against the per-exercise AI image tracker /
                         Exercise Thumbnails manifest). Eligible for production-mode generation.
  'dev_only'          -- tagging complete, but media is not yet hosted (a local file exists but
                         `thumbnail_manifest.csv` has no `image_url` for it). MUST NOT appear in a production-mode
                         generated workout. See MEDIA_GAPS below for the current list and why each is blocked.

Movement `role` (used by the blueprint/adapter for slot-filling and swap eligibility):
  'anchor'    -- complexity 5, or Dumbbell Man Maker specifically (Wes: Man Maker should dominate/anchor the session
                 when selected -- never paired with another heavy compound in the same block). `anchor_exclusive`
                 marks the one exercise (Man Maker) with that hard constraint; other complexity-5 anchors are
                 strongly weighted as block leads but not hard-exclusive.
  'primary'   -- primary_compound in the frozen slot-class vocabulary: a main-block lead movement.
  'secondary' -- secondary_compound only: accessory / unilateral / support work.

`target_class` (which body target this exercise is eligible for): 'upper' | 'lower' | 'full'. Derived from whether
primary muscles fall in the frozen engine's own UPPER / LOWER muscle sets (`engines.strength.audit_engine.UPPER/LOWER`);
pure-core / rotational / combined movements default to 'full'.
"""
